{
  "reasoning": "The defendant contracted a renovation project, received the full payment, and left the site. He only partially paid the workers and owed them over 57,000 yuan. After being ordered by the labor bureau to pay the outstanding wages, he evaded the order and refused to pay, which constitutes the crime of refusing to pay labor remuneration. He later paid the wages, but the refusal and evasion constitute the offense. No other facts support additional charges such as fraud or refusal to execute a civil judgment.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]拒不支付劳动报酬<eoa>"
}
